💥Five people, including three USPS mail carriers in Houston, have been federally charged in an alleged nearly six-year scheme to steal and sell more than $23 million in checks.

💥Prosecutors say postal workers were recruited to pull checks from the mail, which were then advertised and sold through an encrypted Telegram group. The largest check cited in the indictment was allegedly worth $1.5 million.
